        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "NiCl2·6H2O (118.5 mg, 0.5 mmol), Dy(OAc)3·4H2O (206 mg, 0.5 mmol), salicylaldehyde (61 mg, 0.5 mmol) and LH3 (103 mg, 0.5 mmol) were added to MeOH (18 ml) in the presence of NEt3 (0.15 ml, 1.0 mmol). The mixture was transferred to a Teflon-lined autoclave (23 ml) and kept at 120 °C for 12 h. After slow cooling to room temperature at 10 °C h−1, olive-green rod-like crystals of 1 were obtained, collected by filtration, washed with Et2O and dried under vacuum.",
